# Bash Configuration Directory

## Overview
This directory contains the complete bash configuration system for the dotfiles repository.

## Directory Structure

### Core Files
- **`bashrc`**: Main bash configuration file (sourced by ~/.bashrc)
- **`profile`**: Login shell configuration (sourced by ~/.bash_profile)
- **`aliases`**: Global aliases and shortcuts
- **`completion`**: Bash completion configuration

### Directories
- **`rc.d/`**: [Library functions](rc.d/README.md) loaded first during bash startup
- **`enabled/`**: [Startup scripts](enabled/README.md) that configure tools and environments
- **`disabled/`**: [Disabled scripts](disabled/README.md) not loaded during startup
- **`tests/`**: [Test scripts](tests/README.md) for validating configuration
- **`core/`**: [Legacy directory](core/README.md) being removed (deprecated)

## Loading Order
1. **`rc.d/`** files are loaded first (library functions)
2. **`enabled/`** files are loaded second (startup scripts)
3. **`aliases`** is loaded last

## Agent Development
For detailed information about each directory's purpose and usage, see the individual README.md files in each subdirectory.

## Installation
This configuration is managed by the dotfiles repository and deployed via the dotfile manager system.

